+# Daily Grind components
+
+Load `components/daily-grind.js` once with a module script. The four native custom elements use open Shadow DOM and require no dependencies or build step. Content remains in the page through slots, so headings, descriptions, and links are still available if JavaScript is disabled.
+
+| Element | Slots | Behavior |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `coffee-card` | `title`, `description`, `action` | Card with a semantic article and equal-height layout. |
+| `coffee-collection` | `heading`, default (cards) | Responsive grid that fits narrow screens. |
+| `coffee-hero` | `heading`, `description`, `action` | Centered hero with a decorative background image. |
+| `grind-navigation` | `brand`, repeated `link` | Primary navigation with a disclosure button at widths of 760px or less. Escape closes the disclosure and returns focus to the button. |
+
+Use real headings and anchors as slot content. Choose heading levels for the surrounding page, and give repeated action links descriptive accessible names. Slot content is authored HTML; components do not interpolate it into templates. Use `data-outlined` on a navigation link for the outlined treatment.
+
+Components inherit the page font and the `--primary`, `--accent`, and other existing color tokens. Set `--hero-image` on `coffee-hero` to override its decorative background, for example with `style="--hero-image: url('/images/coffee.jpg')"`. Keep meaningful image content in page markup with appropriate alternative text.
+
+Navigation listeners are installed on connection and removed on disconnection, allowing elements to be removed and reinserted. Each navigation instance keeps its disclosure state and control references within its own shadow root. Links retain normal browser navigation and keyboard behavior; the disclosure does not use application-menu roles or trap focus.
